# Show Production by active player

Replace the Production tab's plan-style checks with resource production metrics for every active player.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Production has exactly All, Brick, Ore, Wheat, Sheep, and Wood rows in that order.
- [x] Custom Production rows and New production check are not shown or creatable; existing stored data remains intact for compatibility.
- [x] Each section has one column per active player in stable colour order.
- [x] The first section meta-header is `Avg production per round`.
- [x] Production accounts for owned settlements once and cities twice on adjacent producing hexes.
- [x] Expected production per roll uses dice probability and is multiplied by active-player count to obtain per-round production.
- [x] All is the sum of the five resource values.
- [x] Swiping right or using the arrow shows `Avg rounds until one produced` with each positive value equal to the inverse of mean production per round; zero production is represented clearly without division by zero.
- [x] Plans tab layout, rows, expansion, creation, and statistics remain otherwise unchanged.
- [x] Production math and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Evidence

- Added pure production metrics for active-player settlements/cities, dice probabilities, round scaling, resource totals, inverse values, and zero handling.
- Replaced only the Production tab body with the active-player matrix and retained stored custom Production data for decoding compatibility.
- Added domain regression coverage and focused Production UI assertions; app, unit-test, and UI-test bundles compile for the iPhone 17 simulator.
- Live execution was blocked while CoreSimulator workers failed to materialize; manual focused verification remains intentionally unchecked.
